@@ -357,6 +357,26 @@ creates folders and deletes - in a container or in a volume
 - Limits: 2,000 entries per folder, text edited up to 256 KiB, downloads up
   to 50 MiB, uploads up to 25 MiB, enforced on the machine. A file keeps
   its owner and mode when it is saved.
+- **Show changes** (0.126.0+) compares the edited text with the file as it
+  is on the machine *now* (a unified diff, at most 2,000 lines shown)
+  before anything is saved.
+- **Saving never overwrites someone else's change** (0.126.0+): the editor
+  remembers the SHA-256 of the version it opened, and the worker reads the
+  file again right before writing. When it differs, nothing is written -
+  the editor comes back with your text kept, the differences against the
+  current version shown, and saving again overwrites that version. The
+  refusal is audited (`machine.docker.file.write` with `conflict`).
+- **Several files or a whole folder** (0.126.0+): pick several files, or a
+  folder (its subfolders kept; the browser sends each file with its path
+  inside the folder). Up to 1,000 files and 25 MiB in all, sent as one tar
+  stream. Every path is checked (no `..`, nothing absolute, no control
+  characters) when the tar is built and again in the worker, which also
+  refuses anything but plain files and folders. Several files are written
+  owned by root (644, folders 755); a single file replacing an existing
+  one still keeps its owner and mode.
+- **Download a folder** (0.126.0+) as `.tar.gz` - a folder's row, or
+  *Download this folder* - with owners and modes, up to 50 MiB before
+  compression (compressed in the worker).
 - Every download and every change is audited (`machine.docker.file.*`).
 
